1087:
The chief of police shall:
(1) Execute all orders and directions of the council;
(2) Abate or remove any nuisance when so directed by the council;
(3) Maintain the peace, good order and tranquility of the city by the enforcement of all municipal ordinances and state laws;
(4) Place upon the docket the names of all persons violating any of the municipal ordinances or state laws and arrest and take into custody all persons who violate any of such ordinances or state laws;
(5) When being advised of any disturbance of the peace or disorderly conduct occurring in any house or place in the city upon his own knowledge, or being advised by any person of such conduct, request admission into the premises for the arrest and removal of the offender, and if such a request is not granted by the person in control or management of the premises then such person having such control shall be deemed to be the offender and shall be subject to the penalty provided by law; and
(6) Under the direction of the city administrator be in charge of the police department, and shall have supervision over the members thereof in the exercise of their powers, duties and authority.
(Code 1976, § 3-1002)

1108:
An applicant shall submit to the city planning commission for approval the final plans, specifications, and reports prepared by a licensed professional engineer or registered architect which shall include the following data:
(1) Plot plan showing:
a. Area and dimensions of tract;
b. Streams, watercourses and any proposed diversions;
c. Contours or original grades and proposed grade changes;
d. Service buildings or other proposed structures;
e. Roads and walkways;
f. Water and sewer lines;
g. Fire hydrants and drinking fountains;
h. Size and arrangement of trailer coach spaces;
i. Playground and open space areas; and
j. Refuse storage stations;
(2) Detail plans and specifications of service buildings, roads, walks and other proposed construction; and
(3) Detail plans and specifications of water supply, sewerage and electrical facilities.
(4) Test results on soil, ground water level, drainage, rock formations, and topography;
(5) Such other plan elements, design standards, and controls as may be deemed reasonably necessary by the planning commission to accomplish the purposes of this chapter.
The planning commission may disapprove, approve or modify the plans in order to assure the development of a manufactured home park in accordance with the purposes of this chapter.
When such development plans have been approved, they shall be certified to the city administrator by the chairman of the planning commission and then submitted to mayor and council for final approval.
(Ord. of 9-1-05)
